{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/443086-demon-questions","id":443086,"title":"Demon Questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-15T14:10:58-07:00","id":443086,"title":"Demon Questions","content":"<b>General</b><br /> - Are there any mechanical areas of Demon to look out for as being troublesome, unbalanced, or requiring a lot of ST arbitration to understand?<br /> - How well do demons play in a mixed group?<br /> <br /> <b>Bolthole</b><br /> - Are the weapons created by the <i>Arsenal </i>effect limited to existing weapons, or can you have like 5L Brass Knuckles?<br /> - Are Explosives within the purview of <i>Arsenal</i>?<br /> - Are weapons with special traits (i.e. Silver) obtainable from <i>Arsenal</i>?<br /> - Just clarifying, absolutely anything or anyone left inside a cover-linked Bolthole when you swap covers is completely obliterated, regardless of their talents?<br /> - Are you limited to five dots per bolthole, or can you exceed more for additional benefits? If you can exceed more, does the penalty to detect the Bolthole accrue beyond -5?<br /> <br /> <b>Cultists</b><br /> - Is it me, or are the benefits granted by the 4 and 5 dot versions of this merit extremely vague? What dicepools do the cultists use for their supernatural merits or to accomplish the &quot;unsavory things&quot;?<br /> - Can you link Cultists to other merits, like Retainer or Staff?<br /> <br /> <b>Embeds</b><br /> - In the case of Embeds penalized by Defense, do penalties and things that lower or negate a target's Defense apply? I.e. Ambushing, the opponent All-Out-Attacking, etc.<br /> - How Hot is the fire created by <i>Combustion</i>?<br /> - Does <i>Efficiency </i>stack with Good Time Management to complete things in 1/4 the time?<br /> - Is <i>Miles Away</i>'s duration effectively unlimited until discharged? If that's the case, is it an effective &quot;was I just targeted by an applicable supernatural power&quot; detector?<br /> - Can you use <i>Momentum </i>on Reflexive actions?<br /> - Does <i>Strike First</i> negate Surprise / Ambush? I.e. can the character apply their Defense against attacks?<br /> - If <i>Right Tool, Right Job</i> is applied to a weapon (improvised or otherwise) do successes add to the weapon's damage rating or to dicerolls made to use the weapon?<br /> - Does <i>Tag and Release</i> function across realms of existence? I.e. can a Demon tag something in the mundane world, walk in the Hedge, and then use this embed to find her way back?<br /> - I'm having a hard time grokking <i>Alibi</i>. From what I gather, the demon essentially creates a sort of duplicate (more psuedo co-location?) of one of their covers (possibly their own cover) and the demon can't be recognized for who they are / that cover while doing whatever they are actually doing. Right? How does this work with recorded media, or if someone was asked to describe who actually did whatever it is the character does while under Alibi?<br /> - Can <i>Diversion </i>be used mid-conversation or mid-combat?<br /> - Does <i>Without a Trace</i> work against various Psychometry or Postcognition-like abilities? Presumably with a Clash of Wills?<br /> - An aside, how has <i>Just Bruised</i> and <i>Knockout Punch</i> been playing out in people's games? They're on my radar as potential problems but...<br /> <br /> <b>Exploits</b><br /> - For Exploits that are Extended Actions, does Efficiency and/or Good Time Management apply?<br /> - Is Breaking an object for <i>Break to Heal</i> part of using the Exploit, or does it have to be done separately? If part of the Exploit, is there a limit to what object(s) can be broken?<br /> - When <i>Demon House</i> ends, where does the Demon appear? Where they first used it? Anywhere inside the building?<br /> - If <i>Echoing Death</i> is under the effects of Efficiency and/or Good Time Management (if this is possible at all) how does that work? Take an instant action, make 2 or 4 rolls as appropriate?<br /> - With <i>Raise Dead</i>, is there any way for a Demon to actually place a spare soul into the corpse? Can he take one of his Covers gained from a Soul Pact and bring them back to &quot;life&quot; like this?<br /> - If the AoE version of <i>Swarm </i>is used, how big is the area? 2^(Primum-1)?<br /> <br /> <b>Demonic Form</b><br /> - Some demonic form traits are described in a way that makes them easily concealable (say, with a pair of sunglasses or a hat). Is there any reason that a Demon can't walk around with a few Demonic Form traits out indefinitely?<br /> - <i>Rivet Arm</i> has unlimited ammunition. Does that mean if you score an exceptional success on Merciless Gunman you kill an unlimited number of targets?<br /> - Am I reading <i>Glory and Terror </i>right? You can reflexively impose Insensate vs several targets with no resist or contested roll?<br /> - How big of a swarm does a demon make when discorporeated with <i>Insect Swarm</i>?<br /> - Does being an <i>Insect Swarm</i> limit the demon's actions in any way?<br /> - Does being inside the area affected by the Swarm Tilt caused by an <i>Insect Swarm</i> count as &quot;touching&quot; for Embeds, Exploits, and Demonic Form powers that require it?<br /> - How does forcing someone into a <i>Memory Theft</i> attempt work? Grapple and it's automatically applied, or do you have to do it as a Move?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T16:41:33-07:00","id":443269,"title":"","content":"I don't have time to answer all the questions, so I'll start with the general ones. The main balancing factor in a Demon game is the God Machine. If not for the God Machine, they could walk around in Demonic Form the whole day and use exploits like there is no tomorrow. Some ST arbitration is needed as the ST has to decide whether the God Machine notices certain types of behavior. You will have to decide in advance how strict you are going to be. Don't forget Demons are spies in hostile territory.<br /> <br /> This is also the main problem in crossover. If your crossover game is not centered on the God Machine, the main balancing factor falls away (unless you decide there is another enitity the Demons are hiding from and that will send hunters when it finds them). Another problem is that Demons sometimes loose or shed their covers, making it hard for their other allies to find them again. Also, when his Vampire and Werewolf friends are under God Machine scrutiny, they cannot change covers, so it becomes very hard for the Demon to associate with them. It is possible to run, but you will have to think about those complications beforehand, and of ways to get the group back together when it happens. Maybe it is possible to hack Infrastructure to make the God Machine forget about the Demon's allies for example.<br /> <br /> But still, it would be fun to run a mixed game, with a Demon who pretends to be another splat.<br /> <br /> <br /> Unrelated I want to note that I find the idea of a Demon with Rivet Arm and Merciless Gunman killing an unlimited number of targets intriguing. As normally the available number of targets is limited, I don't think it is a problem under normal circumstances. Especially because the same is possible when wielding a weapon with a clip size in the hundreds, like a belt fed machine gun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T17:23:42-07:00","id":443385,"title":"","content":"Arsenal:<br /> Arsenal says the weapons are mundane but effective, so I would say you have pull weapons that normally or at least reasonably exist.Explosives would of course be limited by the damage scope under the merit, but I would say again a plausible explosive would work. Specific things might require ST approval and no promises you won't get backlash in some form from things you pull though. So you'd have to ask the ST on if its ok to pull a silver knife out of your arsenal or something.<br /> Well things in a cover linked bolthole aren't specifically obliterated, just they cease to be there and demons have yet to figure out where they go. Otherwise yeah anything you leave in there that wasn't part of the initial setup goes bye-bye. As for pushing it beyond 5 the core doesn't list any specific means to do so. Which means you would have to get permission from your ST, and things that result from it are also at the ST's ruling.<br /> <br /> Cult:<br /> 4-5 are considerably high ranked, so the vagaries are meant to make it less limited since this is meant to be a considerable high end power that was hard won. Basically they function as staff, resources, or allies once a story. So as far as dice pool I would say its basically you put out the call and get someone with the right skills that the requested job would require for that level. Stigmatics and supernatural merits are gonna need to be discussed with your ST you have them, but you'll probably need to work out the specifics beyond things like having an information trade with the vampire spying on your cult.<br /> You might be able to get some of the other merits you list out of cult members, but I would personally not allow a direct link where having a 5 dot cult counts as always having a 5 dot staff or something.<br /> <br /> Oh and on the rivet arm, no obviously you can't kill an unlimited number of targets. Eventually you run out of people to kill and then you need to move on to the next massacre site. Then you make it a movie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T00:23:25-07:00","id":443836,"title":"","content":"Embeds:<br /> The fire on combustion probably isn't too hot. Like I would view it as the same heat for say setting wood on fire. Essentially while you can use it to burn things that wouldn't normally be prone to burning just because say I caused a metal door to ignite doesn't mean the fire is hot enough to melt unaltered metal.<br /> Efficiency halves the time for the entire action whereas Good Time Management halves the time between rolls. You could get projects done fast with both (assuming the merit applies to the action), however you would still be counting on getting good enough rolls to pass the project.<br /> As a reflexive embed I would say it only works for the situation in which it was triggered. For example if someone nailed your arm to a table the embed would activate and ,hopefully, allow to deal with the pain until you can remove the nails and perform basic treatment. Since it has to be triggered by pain or serious distraction I would say you can't use it as an always on tripwire for supernatural effects.<br /> I would say it can in theory, but because reflexive actions are defined as happening on an instinctual level I would say it generally does not apply.<br /> Strike First does allow you to act in the same round as the ambush, so I would say if you succeed that it could counter an ambush. However, I will say that you would have to be ruled as at least getting the reflexive action on it. As a result someone a person turning out from around the corner and shoots you then you can use the embed to try and protect yourself. It would not apply if your enemy were to take a sniper shot at your head that you didn't know was coming then it wouldn't apply.<br /> Personally I would say Right Tools, Right Job is not an embed for making weapons. The idea being that the intention I get from the embed is it allows one to use a tool in a way different than how the tool normally would work.<br /> Alibi only covers you during the scene its activated in. It doesn't make it so you can't be recognized it basically makes it so actions contrary to that cover don't apply to said cover. For example, the cover you establish the alibi for is a known pacifist and the action you take after the alibi is established is shooting a person in the face. Obviously this would be a compromise check, but with Alibi up this is handled as someone else being mistaken for the cover because you were clearly having a pleasant chat with some people at the library. Now if at a later scene someone were to investigate footage of this and basically get a positive ID on your cover then compromise can apply as normal. So it gives you some wiggle room to do something abnormal, but not enough to go full out crazy with it.<br /> I don't see too much of an issue with using Diversion during those situations.<br /> I would say supernatural abilities like Post-Cognition could theoretically bypass Without a Trace, however I would probably put the difficulty of the attempt to use that skill as matching the successes from the embed's use.<br /> I can't speak for Just Bruised, but I imagine if you're worried about Knockout Punch just make it clear to your players before hand that it doesn't work on more resilient targets aka named or story significant targets.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T20:31:41-07:00","id":445283,"title":"","content":"Exploits:<br /> The merit <i>Good Time Management</i> I would say doesn't apply to exploits. See <i>Good Time Management</i> is a merit that requires two dots in either science or academics and with the wording on the merits description it sounds less like managing the primium and forces that are occasionally used in exploits and more of your just good at balancing a schedule and all the things normally needed to complete a project. Basically the merit seems like it would only apply to mundane things. Efficiency is fair game though if it is ruled that the exploit actually requires time to accumulate those successes. Like if it were a ritual or something.<br /> <br /> <i>Break to Heal</i> says you need to touch the target and break the object at the same time so it is part of the exploit. I would say you can't break more than one object with it, but if you had a means to say demolish a building with your other hand when you activated the exploit I would say it could work. So I mean it kind of falls to within reason, and I would say the bigger the destroyed object the bigger the metaphorical ping is and so the potential for a cover break becomes larger.<br /> <br /> I would say appearing anywhere inside the structure is fair game for when you break the merger on <i>Demon House</i>.<br /> <br /> <i>Echoing Death </i>doesn't seem like it would be effected since I just don't feel its actually doing any kind of action which can be enhanced. If your ST was willing to say it could work then I might then I would say it would be <i>Efficiency</i> and you would get to make two rolls a turn instead of one, buts that assumes your ST is willing to let you use them at all.<br /> <br /> The description on <i>Raise Dead</i> explicitly says another soul will do if the old isn't available, as well as the fact that the dramatic failure is putting something else into the corpse. You can't technically bring back someone who lost their body due to a soul pact being triggered. This is because the soul is annihilated when the soul pact is called in, so there is no soul to put in anywhere else. Now if your ST wanted to say that the soul was still there or say if the contract was destroyed the soul would exist then its a different story.<br /> <br /> I would say talk to you ST on how big a swarm of whatever you summon is I'm not seeing any rules for it. If you wanted to you could look up how big a swarm of that creature would normally fill in the real world and use that as your base. I'm just not seeing any rules on figuring it myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3400,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","user":"nalak42","date":". 03-17-2015, 06:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T01:47:38-07:00","id":445477,"title":"","content":"Here's a question I'd like to add for anyone to comment on:<br /> <br /> The Glory and Terror form power let's a demon put the Insensate Tilt on people, but the tilt itself says it can be mind blanking fear or pleasure overload.<br /> Can a Demon choose which type of Insensate they cause?<br /> If the consensus is &quot;only the fear type,&quot; would you allow a Demon that also has Inhuman Beauty apply the pleasure overload type?<br /> Additionally, though Insensate is a tilt, do you just consider it a condition if it's applied outside of a combat situation?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thread Reaper <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\">\uff1c(\u00b4 \u055e)\u0a0a( \u055e )\uff1e\ufeff</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/377-xanandithras","name":"Xanandithras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar377_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"427"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T07:11:11-07:00","id":445772,"title":"","content":"I think this is a case where the actual source of the tilt (Glory and Terror) overrides the Insensate Tilt itself. Insensate can be caused by fear or pleasure, but in the case of G&amp;T, its specifically being caused by fear. Glory and Terror is all about scarying people, intimidate bonuses, Hard Leverage/threats, and so on. It doesn't make sense, to me, for G&amp;T to provide pleasure.<br /> <br /> If the Demon has Inhuman Beauty as well, it has nothing to do with the Insensate tilt from the Glory and Terror bit. Nothing says that you can't both be scary and inspiring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T08:46:47-07:00","id":445998,"title":"","content":"I see no reason why Glory and Terror <i>couldn't</i> be used for pleasure as well as fear since it's a fairly common thought that angelic visitation can cause great overwhelming emotional responses of relief, love and adoration (see the Ecstasy of Saint Teresa). In the case of using it to create pleasure and focusing on the Glory more than the Terror, you <i>may</i> want to change the dice pool (perhaps Presence + Persuasion) but this isn't strictly necessary as not all forms of intimidation are necessarily stressful, one can intimidate by being impressive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T11:31:45-07:00","id":446297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DesolateDolly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/443086-demon-questions?p=445998#post445998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the case of using it to create pleasure and focusing on the Glory more than the Terror, you <i>may</i> want to change the dice pool (perhaps Presence + Persuasion) but this isn't strictly necessary as not all forms of intimidation are necessarily stressful, one can intimidate by being impressive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its interesting to note that the dice pool for Inhuman Beauty is also Presence + Intimidation (vs. Composure).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thread Reaper <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\">\uff1c(\u00b4 \u055e)\u0a0a( \u055e )\uff1e\ufeff</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/377-xanandithras","name":"Xanandithras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar377_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"427"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T15:06:46-07:00","id":446590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanandithras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/443086-demon-questions?p=445477#post445477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a question I'd like to add for anyone to comment on:<br /> <br /> The Glory and Terror form power let's a demon put the Insensate Tilt on people, but the tilt itself says it can be mind blanking fear or pleasure overload.<br /> Can a Demon choose which type of Insensate they cause?<br /> If the consensus is &quot;only the fear type,&quot; would you allow a Demon that also has Inhuman Beauty apply the pleasure overload type?<br /> Additionally, though Insensate is a tilt, do you just consider it a condition if it's applied outside of a combat situation?</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Glory and Terror </i>seems to work through the option of just causing terror. While insensate can be caused through pleasure or terror, but <i>Glory and Terror </i>operates along the terror venue. Think of it like knocking a person out by drugging them, or pummeling them into unconsciousness, the outcome is the same just the method used for obtaining it is different. <br /> <br /> That being said I would agree with DesolateDolly that I don't see why you couldn't use it for the pleasure approach. Though I would say that since its a form attribute it would have to be something you okay with your ST when you design the demon so that it is understood that your demon tends to default to just being so amazingly glorious that people tend to almost break from the shear awe of it as opposed to pants wetting terror.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T21:15:23-07:00","id":447095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/443086-demon-questions#post443086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Demonic Form</b><br /> - Some demonic form traits are described in a way that makes them easily concealable (say, with a pair of sunglasses or a hat). Is there any reason that a Demon can't walk around with a few Demonic Form traits out indefinitely?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well you would risk a breach in cover every time one was noticed even if they're easy to hide, and I would argue that most are alien enough that being noticed has a serious chance of causing compromise when seen as a balance for them being easily concealed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/443086-demon-questions#post443086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Am I reading <i>Glory and Terror </i>right? You can reflexively impose Insensate vs several targets with no resist or contested roll?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would argue this only applies to extras any significant characters would get a chance to resist or contest the roll.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/443086-demon-questions#post443086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- How big of a swarm does a demon make when discorporeated with <i>Insect Swarm</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div> Depends on the demon's size. A demon who's natural form is 3 cubic feet is probably going to be significantly less terrifying as a cloud of bugs than the demon who's natural form can be the megazord fight in Power Rangers.<br /> Considering the mention on health levels in the swarm tilt and the power you could say the swarm that is the demon is as big as the demon's health levels.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/443086-demon-questions#post443086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Does being an <i>Insect Swarm</i> limit the demon's actions in any way?</div> </div> </div> </div>While you've dissempbled yourself into a swarm you can't do things beyond the capability of a swarm, so you can use it to get places or attack people but you can't open a door.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/443086-demon-questions#post443086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Does being inside the area affected by the Swarm Tilt caused by an <i>Insect Swarm</i> count as &quot;touching&quot; for Embeds, Exploits, and Demonic Form powers that require it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but you would be dealing with the fact that triggering them is probably going to be harder than normal since you're trying to affect something composed of an insane amount of parts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/443086-demon-questions#post443086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- How does forcing someone into a <i>Memory Theft</i> attempt work? Grapple and it's automatically applied, or do you have to do it as a Move?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that the grapple is basically attempting to force the connection, so if you succeed at the grapple then it is basically that you managed to overpower the person well enough to gain access.<br /> <br /> Hope these have been helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T01:29:19-07:00","id":447379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DesolateDolly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/443086-demon-questions?p=445998#post445998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see no reason why Glory and Terror <i>couldn't</i> be used for pleasure as well as fear since it's a fairly common thought that angelic visitation can cause great overwhelming emotional responses of relief, love and adoration (see the Ecstasy of Saint Teresa). In the case of using it to create pleasure and focusing on the Glory more than the Terror, you <i>may</i> want to change the dice pool (perhaps Presence + Persuasion) but this isn't strictly necessary as not all forms of intimidation are necessarily stressful, one can intimidate by being impressive.</div> </div> </div> </div>. I think, if you reallywant to do this, you should just make a new demon form. I find it very strange that the other benefits revolve around evoking fear (inimidate bonus, hard leverage) would be combined with invoking pleasure. It feels... Inconsistent. And consistency is important to storytelling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T17:31:58-07:00","id":448529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/443086-demon-questions?p=447379#post447379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. I think, if you reallywant to do this, you should just make a new demon form. I find it very strange that the other benefits revolve around evoking fear (inimidate bonus, hard leverage) would be combined with invoking pleasure. It feels... Inconsistent. And consistency is important to storytelling.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see anything inconsistent with &quot;Holy Ecstasy&quot; being used in place of &quot;Holy Terror&quot;, as both would be Intimidation rolls (this benefits from the +3 Intimidation bonus). Both are present in the Insensate Tilt. Both would be Hard Leverage. Just as you would use supernaturally invoked fear to push a mortal to do as you want, you would also use supernaturally invoked ecstasy to get them to do what you want. It is consistent with all rolls within the power and with the Insensate tilt itself <i>and</i> with angelic themes. Intense pleasure can be sensually overwhelming so as to be considered intimidating. <i>If</i> you decided that ecstatic sensations <i>couldn't</i> be used to intimidate, which I disagree with but that's your call, then yes you'd have to make another power or expand this one to include another set of bonus/rolls to include the possibility of that. However since it's called <i>Glory</i> and Terror I believe that implies both fear and pleasure can be used to intimidate an unprepared human being.<br /> <br /> It's also worth noting that, for example, when Moses descends from Mt. Sinai his fear and awe were painted on his face. He had beheld the glory of God and had that affect him with both awe and fear. In the context of the power carrying this theme I think the power is invoking both intense awe and intense horror at the same time and that it's really up to the storyteller what, if not both, would be the trappings of the Insensate tilt. However, at the end of the day, &quot;pleasure&quot; and &quot;horror&quot; are not mechanical terms they are narrative trappings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T00:04:24-07:00","id":448895,"title":"","content":"I think we may be conflating &quot;glory and wonder&quot; and &quot;pleasure&quot; a bit too much in this conversation. Road to Domascus moment by makign people fall face down from your glory and their respect in holy rapture? Yes.<br /> <br /> Insensate through aoe spontanious orgasm? Lame.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T01:13:51-07:00","id":448924,"title":"","content":"While the Ecstasy of Saint Teresa might amuse some for its latter implications, I rather think the insensate tilt is applicable to both, though I was referring to the former.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T06:12:11-07:00","id":449066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/443086-demon-questions?p=448895#post448895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we may be conflating &quot;glory and wonder&quot; and &quot;pleasure&quot; a bit too much in this conversation. Road to Domascus moment by makign people fall face down from your glory and their respect in holy rapture? Yes.<br /> <br /> Insensate through aoe spontanious orgasm? Lame.</div> </div> </div> </div> I actually consider awe and wonder to be a form of fear and surprise (note that, since I thought that, I file religious excasty here automatically), while pleasure to be from, ah, well orgasm would do it, but I was thinking of something more like a drug induced high, all the pleasure centers of your brain being tickled at once. Nothing wrong with the former, but the latter? I just don't think it should happen with this demon form.<br /> <br /> But that's all just going to come down to arguing over what &quot;pleasure&quot; is. Apparently, we weren't all on the same page with it, and I thought we kinda were. If we're just getting into a semantics argument over what Religious Excasty should fall under, well, definitely time to drop the subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 03-19-2015, 09:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}